# The mecha module a prerelease published from this branch pins (see
# workflows/prerelease-gcp.yml): mecha-fork's host launch synced onto upstream mecha
# 0.22.0 (feat/host-launch-0.17, mecha-fork#22) with the preset-enforcing imgproxy stand-in (mecha-fork#24), the airlock door (#26) and a provider's sign-in adopting the guest it starts from (mecha-fork#28), a door caller naming the sink's Idempotency-Key (#30), a guest's token refresh (#31), a door's own timeoutMs and hashed headers (#34), API keys behind capabilities.apiKeys (#36), auth's handoff codes spent in the database (#38) and its keyExchanged hook (#41), published by workflows/prerelease-mecha.yml. Its host.14 adds an app's schemas (meta.schema, #Tenancy), auth's POST /auth/upgrade and the door's environment (meta.doorEnvironment); host.15, the host's Electric serving an app's own schema and floor (mecha-fork#45); host.17, the bounded cdc-events stream (#46) and a host peer that is itself a bayt target reached through bayt (#47, #48).
# 0.25.0-host.1: that line synced onto upstream mecha 0.25.0 (mecha-fork#53).
MECHA_V=0.25.0-host.1
# The omnishell module and runtime it pins: omnishell-fork line/0.23.0-fork, upstream
# omnishell 0.23.0 with line/0.20.3 (fork.18) carried onto it (omnishell-fork#27) and
# the speculation-rules split upstream's shell no longer has (omnishell-fork#29),
# published by workflows/prerelease-omnishell.yml; fork.3 bundles interpreter/vendor/mecha-client.js,
# which 0.23's tree no longer carries; fork.8 keeps a guest across visits (#34) and fork.10 hands it to a
# provider's sign-in (#36); fork.11 refreshes a kept guest's token before it runs out (#37).  fork.14 serves the renderer's /ready (#40); fork.13 was cut without the mecha-client bundle and is not to be used. fork.15 logs a refused service-worker registration rather than failing boot (#42); fork.16 adds data-text-format="money" (#43).
# 0.25.0-fork.1: line/0.25.0-fork, the fork line synced onto upstream omnishell 0.25.0 (omnishell-fork#48).
OMNISHELL_V=0.25.0-fork.1
